From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:20:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] chat links: pin the profile-board dedup, origin
 filter and unlinked-chat count

Post-merge check t_01a1d5b4a18ea0f8 of PR #2372 ran exact-anchor mutants on
hermes_cli/kanban_chat_links.py; three survived the chat-links suites, so these
clauses had no test:

- C5 `_merge_profile_board`: without `ref not in have`, a replica row of the same
  chat/owner gateway/board/id (here: a link whose card row is missing) no longer
  dedups the ledger's profile-board copy; it replaces the replica's answer or,
  under another owner label, lists the card twice.
- C8 `_profile_board_cards`: without the origin_gateway / origin_profile filter,
  another gateway's or origin profile's chat's profile-board cards leak into this
  reader for the same session id.
- C10 `links_diff`: without popping skipped chats from `profile_board`, a
  placeholder/machine chat's profile-board card counts in profile_board_links.

Test-only: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_chat_links_profile_board_pins.py (new
file, so it does not touch the files PR #2415 edits).

Proof (sdlc-review scripts/mutants.py; files run: the new pins +
test_kanban_chat_links.py + test_kanban_run_machine.py):
- main 523ecc3ac9b: baseline 45 passed; C5, C8, C8a (gateway clause only),
  C8b (profile clause only), C10 all killed, each by its own new test.
- PR #2415 head 92dacc9084 (+ this file, + its profile_board suite): baseline
  50 passed; C5, C8, C10 killed.

Card: t_01a1d5e24b63d688
